{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Justice, justice you shall pursue.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it warns that a person should be just in his deeds and in his words, for these are the things through which a person can do harm to himself and to others, and therefore the duplication of expression comes. And whoever is just in his words is a sign and proof of the righteousness of his deeds, and therefore it is proper for each and every one of Israel to be just in speech and in deed, as it is written (Zephaniah 3:13): ״שארית ישראל לא יעשו עולה ולא ידברו כזב״. Or the verse may be speaking to the people who have the dispute and warn them to pursue justice whether for gain or for loss, and this is the duplication of expression." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: ״צדק צדק תרדוף״ — tzedek that receives from tzedek, pursue: when you execute justice in your own court. And in the manner of what is written (Exodus 15:16): ״תפול עליהם אימתה ופחד״ — אימתה is the final Hei in the Name that receives from פחד. And so you will find in Sefer ha-Bahir: What is ״צדק צדק״, twice? He said to him: for it is written (II Samuel 22:13) ״מנגה נגדו״ — the first tzedek is tzedek itself; this is Shekhinah, as it is said (Isaiah 1:21): ״צדק ילין בה״. What is the second tzedek? This is the tzedek that instills fear in the righteous, and this tzedek is one who sets salvation as a crown on his head, and ראש is nothing but אמת, as it is said (Psalms 119:160): ״ראש דברך אמת״, and אמת is nothing but שלום, as it is said (II Kings 20:19): ״כי שלום ואמת יהיה בימי״ — end of quotation. And for this reason we find that the masters of truth call a convert who comes to take refuge under the wings of the Shekhinah a גר צדק." "<b>That you may live.</b> In the World to Come, in the supernal tzedek, which is the great light hidden away for the righteous. <b>And you shall inherit the land.</b> In the lower tzedek, in the Land of Israel, corresponding to it. And to this intention Solomon said (Proverbs 21:21): ״רודף צדקה וחסד ימצא חיים צדקה וכבוד״ — he explained that if a person pursues the attribute of judgment included within mercy, which is called חסד ה׳, he will find supernal tzedek, which is the life of the World to Come; this is ״ימצא חיים צדקה וכבוד״. And this is clear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:56.694632800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}